<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thousand Days' War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1899–1902</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thousand Days' War was a civil war in Colombia from 1899 to 1902 between the governing Conservatives and the Liberals, which killed perhaps 100,000 people. Much of the final fighting took place on the isthmus of Panama, then a Colombian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>, and the war ended with treaties signed in 1902, one of them aboard the American battleship USS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a>. The devastation it left helped make possible Panama's secession in 1903.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thousand-days-war.jpg" alt="Thousand Days' War" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: henry duperly · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banquete2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
